Include the Intel denormal-operand exception in FE_ALL_EXCEPT.

Source: Libm-2026 (17a5f9daa3f5679f7536b26f133b40cc078753c3), Source/Intel/fenv.h.
Scope: macOS SDK 26.0 and 26.5, x86_64.

Apple architecture-282 i386/fpu.h and Intel's x87 and MXCSR documentation
establish bit 1. The consumer spelling is corroborated by Remill. The C
fixture checks the spelling, value and inclusion in FE_ALL_EXCEPT.

Evidence: recipes/README.md and .agents/skills/review-macos-c-sdk/scripts/sdk_review/headers/fixtures/c_interfaces/fenv_denorm_mask.c.

--- a/usr/include/architecture/i386/fenv.h
+++ b/usr/include/architecture/i386/fenv.h
@@ -95,7 +95,8 @@
 #define FE_OVERFLOW         0x0008
 #define FE_DIVBYZERO        0x0004
 #define FE_INVALID          0x0001
-#define FE_ALL_EXCEPT       0x003D
+#define FE_DENORMALOPERAND  (1 << 1) /* MXCSR and x87 denormal operand flag */
+#define FE_ALL_EXCEPT       (0x003D | FE_DENORMALOPERAND)
 
 /*    Definitions of rounding direction macros                                */
 #define FE_TONEAREST        0x0000
